              "answer": 1,
              "explanation": "Correct mapping: A–2, B–1, C–3. The ovule contains the megasporangium or nucellus surrounded by an integument. The nucellus is the megasporangial tissue within the ovule. A diploid megaspore mother cell undergoes meiosis to form haploid megaspores.",
